  "review": {
    "note": "Reviewed all direct build, runtime, optional/development and Node dependencies against fresh PyPI/npm discovery, the prior receipt and the installed Python 3.14 environment. The only new candidate is build 1.6.1. Reviewed https://github.com/pypa/build/blob/1.6.1/CHANGELOG.rst and https://github.com/pypa/build/compare/1.6.0...1.6.1: the Windows isolated-venv symlink fix is outside our --no-isolation path, while explicit editable/sdist/wheel dispatch preserves our supported sdist/wheel calls. PyPI metadata requires Python >=3.10 and explicitly supports 3.14. Upgraded local build from 1.6.0 to 1.6.1 and successfully built the 0.21.2 sdist and wheel using .venv/bin/python -m build --no-isolation --outdir /private/tmp/h2hdb-ingest-build-1.6.1. Every other latest candidate is unchanged and matches the installed environment. All candidates satisfy existing bounds and Python candidates support 3.14; no dependency manifest changes are needed. Targeted CLI/process logging, storage/maintenance and real EXIF warning regressions passed; filter on/off preserves CBZ bytes, evidence, source hashes and policy fingerprint with one and four page workers. Native candidate diagnostics cover the complete 16-worker bound. Manual H2HDB_TEST_MARIADB=1 .venv/bin/pytest -o addopts= --strict-markers -m \"mariadb and deep\" -n 0 -q tests/test_runtime_process_lifecycle.py passed all four MariaDB 10.11.11 cases. API/config/schema/exit codes, qualification and retry behavior remain compatible; whole-line log parsers must permit added fields. The merge gate separately validates the final candidate and installed-wheel smoke.",
    "status": "reviewed"
  },
